"use strict";(self.webpackChunkdatabricks_monolith=self.webpackChunkdatabricks_monolith||[]).push([[43209],{43209:e=>{e.exports='# Find Case Events\n\nHow to get **events** for a specific Lakewatch case — **notables** for a security case or **operational alerts** for a system case. Use when the user asks to see events, notables, findings, or alerts for a case (e.g. "show events for this case", "what notables are in case X?", "list alerts for system case Y").\n\n## Security case: list notables\n\nWhen the user has a **security case** ID (from **apiListLakewatchSecurityCases** or **apiGetLakewatchResourceById** with `resourceType: "security-case"`), call **apiListLakewatchSecurityCaseNotables**.\n\n| Parameter | Required | Description                                    |\n| --------- | -------- | ---------------------------------------------- |\n| `caseId`  | Yes      | The security case UUID.                        |\n| `limit`   | No       | Max notables to return (default 100, max 500). |\n\n## System case: list events\n\nWhen the user has a **system case** ID (from **apiListLakewatchSystemCases** or **apiGetLakewatchResourceById** with `resourceType: "system-case"`), call **apiListLakewatchSystemCaseEvents**.\n\n| Parameter | Required | Description                                  |\n| --------- | -------- | -------------------------------------------- |\n| `caseId`  | Yes      | The system case UUID.                        |\n| `limit`   | No       | Max events to return (default 100, max 500). |\n\n**Requirements:** A SQL warehouse must be running; otherwise the tool returns an error asking the user to start one.\n\n## When to use other approaches\n\n- **Find or open a case** (to get its ID) → [find-security-case.md](find-security-case.md) or [find-system-case.md](find-system-case.md), or **apiGetLakewatchResourceById** with `resourceType: "security-case"` or `"system-case"`.\n- **Schema or ad-hoc query of the notables table** (e.g. by rule ID, time range) → **apiGetLakewatchConfig** for table location, then **readTable** / **executeSql**.\n- **Navigate to a case** → use the navigation skill.\n'}}]);
